Step-by-step (Ubuntu 20.04/22.04/24.04 on EC2)

1.Connect & update

sudo apt-get update -y && sudo apt-get install -y ca-certificates curl gnupg lsb-release


2.(Recommended) Ensure time sync

sudo apt-get install -y chrony
sudo systemctl enable --now chrony || sudo systemctl enable --now chronyd


3.Install Java 17 (required by current Jenkins LTS)

sudo apt-get install -y openjdk-17-jre
java -version   # should show version "17"


4.Add the official Jenkins repository

sudo mkdir -p /etc/apt/keyrings
curl -fsSL https://pkg.jenkins.io/debian-stable/jenkins.io-2023.key | sudo tee /etc/apt/keyrings/jenkins-keyring.asc >/dev/null
echo "deb [signed-by=/etc/apt/keyrings/jenkins-keyring.asc] https://pkg.jenkins.io/debian-stable binary/" | sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/jenkins.list >/dev/null
sudo apt-get update -y


5.Install Jenkins

sudo apt-get install -y fontconfig jenkins


6.Start & enable on boot

sudo systemctl enable --now jenkins
sudo systemctl status jenkins --no-pager

7.Grab the initial admin password & open Jenkins

sudo cat /var/lib/jenkins/secrets/initialAdminPassword

9.Open: http://<EC2-PUBLIC-IP>:8080 → paste the password → “Install suggested plugins” → create admin user.
